---
import InsertLayout from '../layouts/InsertLayout.astro';
---

<InsertLayout
  title="Toledo Partner"
  description="White-label engineering for agencies, studios, and consultancies, with contractual non-solicitation boundaries and written IP terms."
  heading="Direct senior capacity, with provenance intact."
  subheading="Toledo Partner is Nicholas Toledo's white-label engineering engagement for agencies, studios, and consultancies. The disclosure model follows your agreement, but authorship, credentials, and delivery history are never fabricated."
>
  <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
    <span class="num">B8</span><span class="bar"></span><span
      >Toledo Partner</span
    >
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>How this works</h2>
    <p>
      You win the work. You lead the design or the strategy. We sit behind your
      team — sometimes in your Slack as Nicholas, sometimes in a private
      delivery channel — and ship the engineering you'd otherwise hire for. Work
      happens in your repos, infrastructure, and accounts. Commits remain
      traceable to their actual author unless an agreed system account is used;
      the engagement never invents a person or credential.
    </p>
    <p>
      The contract has three things in it: a standard NDA; assignment of the
      completed deliverables defined in the proposal after final payment; and a
      non-solicitation clause that prohibits us from soliciting your client
      during the engagement and for two years after. Toledo retains general
      methods, reusable components, and internal tools unless the agreement says
      otherwise. These are terms offered for future work, not a claim about a
      long history of partner engagements.
    </p>
    <p>
      Pricing is hourly or retainer, your choice. Hourly is simpler for one-off
      projects; retainers make sense once we know your team's cadence and your
      pipeline.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section id="rate-card">
    <h2>Rate card</h2>
    <div
      class="data-table-scroll"
      role="region"
      aria-label="Partner rate card; scroll horizontally on a small screen"
      tabindex="0"
    >
      <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 24px 0;">
        <thead>
          <tr
            style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--gf-ink-200); text-align: left;"
          >
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Tier</th>
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Rate</th>
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Best for</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"
              ><strong>White-label development</strong></td
            >
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$125/hr</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">Committed bulk engineering capacity</td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"
              ><strong>Complex / architecture subcontract</strong></td
            >
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$150–$175/hr</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;"
              >Auth, data, AI, and complex architecture</td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Technical audit</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$2,500/project</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;"
              >Pre-acquisition or pre-launch codebase review</td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Emergency overflow</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$300/hr</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">Deadline rescue; four-hour minimum</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>Retainer options for partners</h3>
    <div
      class="data-table-scroll"
      role="region"
      aria-label="Partner retainers; scroll horizontally on a small screen"
      tabindex="0"
    >
      <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 24px 0;">
        <thead>
          <tr
            style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--gf-ink-200); text-align: left;"
          >
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Plan</th>
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Monthly</th>
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Hours</th>
            <th style="padding: 12px;">Effective rate</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Partner Lite</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$2,500/mo</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">20 hrs</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$125/hr</td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Partner Standard</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$5,000/mo</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">40 hrs</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$125/hr</td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-100);">
            <td style="padding: 12px;"><strong>Partner Plus</strong></td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$10,000/mo</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">80 hrs</td>
            <td style="padding: 12px;">$125/hr</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <h2>What we do well as a partner</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Next.js / React frontend</strong> — including art-directed work, scroll
        choreography, complex state, accessibility
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Backend / APIs</strong> — Node, Python, Go, REST and GraphQL, Postgres,
        queueing, background jobs
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>AI integration</strong> — RAG systems, agent infrastructure, governance,
        deterministic replay, cost controls
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>DevOps / CI/CD</strong> — Vercel, Cloudflare, AWS, GitHub Actions
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Code rescues</strong> — taking over abandoned codebases, modernizing
        legacy work
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Discovery support</strong> — joining scoped calls as the named technical
        contributor
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <h2>The non-solicitation, in plain English</h2>
    <p>
      The standard term we offer covers the engagement and <strong
        >two years after the last invoice</strong
      >. The signed agreement controls the exact boundary. Under that term, we
      will not:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Solicit your client directly through any channel</li>
      <li>
        Reference your client by name in our portfolio without your written
        approval
      </li>
      <li>Solicit your employees or contractors</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section id="inquire">
    <h2>Inquire as a Partner</h2>
    <form
      action="https://eolkits.com/api/v1/lead"
      method="POST"
      class="intake-form"
      style="display: grid; gap: 24px; max-width: 600px;"
    >
      <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="New Partner Inquiry" />
      <input
        type="hidden"
        name="source"
        value="toledotechnologies.com/partner"
      />
      <input type="hidden" name="product" value="Toledo Partner" />
      <input
        type="hidden"
        name="context"
        value="White-label engineering inquiry"
      />
      <input
        type="hidden"
        name="_next"
        value="https://toledotechnologies.com/partner?submitted=true"
      />
      <input type="hidden" name="_honey" style="display:none" />

      <fieldset
        style="border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-200); padding: 24px; display: grid; gap: 16px;"
      >
        <legend style="padding: 0 8px; font-weight: bold;"
          >About your agency</legend
        >
        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;"
          >Agency / studio name <input
            type="text"
            name="agency_name"
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          /></label
        >
        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;"
          >Website <input
            type="url"
            name="agency_website"
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          /></label
        >
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset
        style="border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-200); padding: 24px; display: grid; gap: 16px;"
      >
        <legend style="padding: 0 8px; font-weight: bold;"
          >About the work</legend
        >
        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;">
          What capacity gap or project should we understand?
          <textarea
            name="notes"
            rows="4"
            placeholder="Describe the work, expected cadence or hours, stack, and disclosure requirements."
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          ></textarea>
        </label>
      </fieldset>

      <fieldset
        style="border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-200); padding: 24px; display: grid; gap: 16px;"
      >
        <legend style="padding: 0 8px; font-weight: bold;">Contact</legend>
        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;"
          >Name <input
            type="text"
            name="name"
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          /></label
        >
        <label style="display: grid; gap: 8px;"
          >Email * <input
            type="email"
            name="email"
            required
            style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-300);"
          /></label
        >
      </fieldset>

      <button
        type="submit"
        style="padding: 16px; background: var(--gf-ink-900); color: white; border: none; cursor: pointer; font-weight: bold;"
        >Submit partner inquiry</button
      >
      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--gf-ink-500);">
        This form posts to Toledo's lead intake service at eolkits.com. Read the
        <a href="/privacy">privacy details</a> and <a href="/terms">terms</a>.
      </p>
    </form>
    <div
      id="submission-success"
      role="status"
      tabindex="-1"
      hidden
      style="margin-top: 32px; padding: 24px; border: 1px solid var(--gf-ink-900); background: var(--gf-paper);"
    >
      <p style="margin: 0;">
        <strong>Inquiry received.</strong> Any reply will come from
        <code>hello@toledotechnologies.com</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section
    class="cta-banner"
    style="background: var(--gf-ink-900); color: white; padding: 48px; text-align: center;"
  >
    <p
      class="meta"
      style="text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; font-size: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;"
    >
      B8 / Outro
    </p>
    <h2 style="font-size: 32px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
      You own the relationship. Nicholas remains accountable for the engineering
      execution. The agreement keeps provenance and boundaries explicit.
    </h2>
    <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; justify-content: center;">
      <a
        href="#inquire"
        style="display: inline-block; padding: 12px 24px; border: 1px solid white; color: white; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;"
        >Inquire as a partner</a
      >
      <a
        href="#rate-card"
        style="display: inline-block; padding: 12px 24px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3); color: white; text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;"
        >See the rate card</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
</InsertLayout>

<script>
  if (new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('submitted') === 'true') {
    const success = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#submission-success');
    if (success) {
      success.hidden = false;
      success.focus();
    }
  }
</script>
